>Yesterday I played a wizard. I was quite happy when I found a ring of
>polymorph and a ring of shock resistance among my initial equipment.
>I removed my cloak to protect it from being torn apart when polymorphing
>and then put both rings on my fingers. At the end of the 1st level the ring
>of polymorph enabled itself. I shuddered for a moment and then died from a
>system shock!

>How can this happen when I am shock resistant?

Because that's the wrong kind of Shock.
Shock resistance is protection from electricity (like the little
grid bugs which zap you.  System shock is a reaction to your body
changing form suddenly (I think RoPC helps you there)

The semantic difference is probably only evident to those you
have been exposed to the D&D game systems.

